  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Agriculture Scaling Diagnostic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to the World Bank&#x2019;s FoodSystems 2030 Trust Fund theme on scaling science, knowledge and innovation (SKI). This aims to identify strategic gaps and catalytic opportunities to scale science-backed innovation, particularly in Africa. The goal is not just to bring innovations to scale in a project, but to work with public and private actors to develop systems and capacity for countries to scale innovations repeatedly and with much greater reach.  The project will implement diagnostics in at least two countries in East and Southern Africa to assess the gaps and opportunities that exist for scaling innovation into country partner processes. In at least one of these countries the project will develop and pilot a Scaling Unit for the development of public and private (and public-private) strategies around selected sustainable agricultural innovations of greatest priority to them.</narrative>
  </description>
